## Findings

- F-QA1 (gate-semantics caveat, NOT a wave defect): `--check-idempotent` compares pass-1 vs pass-2
  into the working tree; it does NOT compare against committed HEAD. Proof: it exited rc=0 while
  leaving 35 generated leaves divergent from HEAD (host npm @openrig/cli@0.7.5 skill content vs
  committed 0.7.4-era snapshot; generator reads skills from global npm root, line 737-741).
  The wave did not cause this (zero generator-input diffs; divergence is environmental and pre-existing
  per Wave-1 "idempotence HOLD-with-deferral" note). Recommendation: future waves either pin the
  skill source for regen or document that post-check `git checkout --` of generated leaves is expected
  on hosts with npm 0.7.5 (as done here and in the self-QA).
- No vacuous acceptance checks found. No overclaims warranting FAIL.

QA verdict: PASS (independent re-review). Final VERDICT ownership stays with drift-guard per handoff §2.
